cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or its results, please cite the VOTS2026 challenge results paper."
title: "DAM4SAM-VOTS2026: training-free SAM2.1 tracker variants and a sequestered-set component ablation"
authors:
  - family-names: Galea
    given-names: Alexandru-Marian
    affiliation: "The National University of Science and Technology Politehnica Bucharest, Romania"
    email: alexandru.galea2000@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/alexxgalea/dam4sam-vots2026"
abstract: >-
  Six training-free tracker variants built on DAM4SAM / SAM2.1, evaluated in the main
  VOTS2026 sub-challenge (ECCV 2026 Workshops). All six exceeded the co-authorship
  baseline; the best (dam4sam_l_cloud) reached Q=0.639, rank 9/25, outperforming the
  committee DAM4SAM entry, and dam4sam_v3g posted NRE=0.035, the third lowest
  not-reported error of all 25 entries. The repository additionally contains a
  seven-variant knock-out ablation scored on the sequestered evaluation set, with
  byte-level verification of stored trajectories, which attributes the measured gain
  to bounded non-conditioning memory and documents a state-estimation deadlock that
  rendered the intended motion module unreachable.
keywords:
  - visual object tracking
  - video object segmentation
  - SAM2
  - VOTS2026
  - ablation study
  - negative results
license: "Apache-2.0"   # original contributions only; see LICENSE for scope
